                for name2 in zfile2.namelist():
                    if name2.lower().endswith('.csv'):
                        with zfile2.open(name2) as f:
                            dfs[name2] = pd.read_csv(f)
```

`dfs` ends up as a dict mapping each CSV name (e.g. `ABC123.csv`) to its DataFrame. If you want the DataFrame keyed by the inner zip name instead, use `name` as the key.

Note: `pd.read_csv(path, compression='zip')` only works when the zip contains exactly one file and you pass it a real path/URL — it can't handle a zip inside a zip, which is why opening the inner member with `zfile2.open(...)` is the right approach.
